gomodel:67c10cc400007163
        a                 owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment      "General: 1. It is not know which enzyme does the H3K9 methylation. Here we propose the three known human ones. Note that SETDB1 is also reads H3K14ac, which may be a UHFR1 ubiquitination target alongside H3K18 and H3K23 (see PubMed: \n29234025). There are also SETDB2, EHMT1 and EHMT2 that could do the H3K9me3 modification.\n2. UHRF1 is both a reader and a writer. Different domains are responsible for reading and writing, so for now we made two separate activity units.\nDNMT1 is both a Histone ubi reader and a DNA 5mC (cytosine) methylase" ;
        lego:modelstate   "development" ;
        dc:contributor    "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1813-6857" , "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8534-6582" ;
        dc:date           "2026-11-27" ;
        dc:title          "UHRF1 Hsap is a histone reader and a ubi ligase" ;
        pav:providedBy    "http://greekc.org" , "http://geneontology.org" ;
        biolink:in_taxon  obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

